+# Run "$@" with the device's own /system (its linker and libraries) visible
+# at /system. A binary built for FireOS rather than statically — magiskpolicy
+# always, and many busybox builds — cannot run in TWRP otherwise: its
+# interpreter is /system/bin/linker, which is the recovery's, not FireOS's.
+# Scoped to the one command, because TWRP's own tools may live in /system.
